  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on the 12th October 2004 the proposed rear extension at 84 Greencroft Road, Hounslow, would be lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe development falls within Class A Part 1 Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the cubic content of the proposed extension and the existing extension would be 69.24m3, which is within the maximum permitted development volume of 70m3 for development to a semi-detached dwelling.\r\n"
